# Demiurge v2 Master Plan: Weeks 2-5 Redo for 49M Model on 234k Data

## What This Document Is

This is the master plan for redoing Weeks 2-5 of Demiurge with the larger 49M parameter model trained on the new 234k Drake-validated scene corpus (v1+v2). Each prior week becomes a phase here, but compressed since most infrastructure already exists.

This is NOT a prompt. It's the planning document. Prompts split off this in a separate pass.

## Context: What We Have vs. What Original Weeks Had

| Resource | Original Weeks 2-5 | This Run |
|---|---|---|
| Training scenes | 50k (built fresh in W2) | 234k (v1 + v2 already on W&B) |
| Model target | 9M (v7 final) | 49M (v9 target) |
| Validator | Built fresh in W1 | Exists, validated, unchanged |
| Procedural sampler | Built fresh in W2 | Exists, used to generate v1+v2 |
| Training scripts | Built fresh in W3 | Exists with v4-v8 configs as reference |
| Text conditioning | Built fresh in W3 | Exists, sentence-transformers embeddings cached |
| Class balancing | Built fresh in W4 | Exists (Phase A v4 fix) — likely skip this run |
| UG infrastructure | Built fresh in W5 | Exists at src/guidance/energy.py |
| Eval harness | Built fresh in W5 | Exists in scripts/run_eval.py |
| VLM judging | Built fresh in W5 | Exists with caching |
| Pareto plotting | Built fresh in W5 | Exists at scripts/plot_pareto.py |

Translation: this isn't really Weeks 2-5 redo. It's "v9 training + re-eval with existing scripts on existing infrastructure." Much faster than original.

## The Three Real Things We're Doing

Stripped of historical baggage:

1. Train v9 unconditional (49M, 234k data, from scratch)
2. Validate it works visually (VLM probe before spending more compute)
3. Train v9 conditional (warm-init from v9 uncond, add text + CFG dropout)
4. Run UG sweep + eval harness on v9
5. Ship Week 6 writeup (LinkedIn, README, demo)

The validation gate after unconditional is your explicit ask. Smart move — prevents burning compute on cond training if uncond is broken.

